If you want to go farther, you're probably ready for the castle at
this point. However, the biggest dangers you may face won't care about
a few extra points of AC.

Get a tonal musical instrument to activate the drawbridge/guillotine;
if you've killed soldiers then you probably have a bugle. Then, make
sure you've got a wand of fire or lightning for engraving when you
head down Medusa's stair, because the castle may contain boss liches.
They can kill you instantly with the "touch of death" unless you found
gray dragon scale mail or a CoMR, or *unless you are standing on a
burnt Elbereth square*. Finally, if there are intermittent maze levels
between medusa and the castle, make sure you have a wand of digging in
inventory. Even a Valk with -20 AC and a +3 weapon faces danger from a
minotaur, so if you encounter one, DIG DOWNWARD.


